# Review: AutomationPlugin (plugin-routine)

The spec describes the earlier AutomationPlugin. The package has since moved to a Routine model.
Triggers belong to a `Routine` and are edited inside `RoutineForm`/`RoutineArticle`, and the only
space-settings surface is `RoutineSettings`, which toggles `triggersDisabled`. `AutomationPanel`,
`FunctionsPanel` and `RoutineProperties` exist nowhere in the repo, and `TriggerEditor` is now
`TriggerSection`/`TriggerForm`. The engine side holds up. `TriggerRuntimeController` drives the
per-space `TriggerDispatcher` from the kill switch. The dispatcher (in `@dxos/compute-runtime`)
handles timer, feed and subscription triggers and skips `remote` ones. `layer-specs.ts` merges
operation handlers, skills and toolkits and contributes `FeedTraceSink` through `makeRoutingSink`.
Force-run is now `RunRoutine`: it routes a remote trigger to the trigger manager, but runs a local
routine's runnable directly rather than through `TriggerDispatcher.invokeTrigger`.
`CreateTriggerFromTemplate` exists but has no test, wires `trigger.runnable` (not `function`) and
navigates to the routines settings path. All the UI scenarios (T-1 to T-5) are missing.

Of 45 items: 9 done, 12 untested, 4 partial, 8 diverged, 12 missing.

## Extensions

| Term      | URI                        |
| --------- | -------------------------- |
| `verdict` | `org.dxos.mdl.verdict@1.0` |

